==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is an [[Aku Altar (Enemy Base)|Aku Altar]].
*Infinite [[Relic Doge]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 60~80 seconds<sup>1,800f~2,400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 60~80 seconds<sup>1,800f~2,400f</sup>.
*1 [[Relic Doge]] spawns after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*1 [[Relic Doge]] spawns after 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.
*1 [[Relic Doge]] spawns after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Aku Doge]] spawns after 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>.
*1 [[Aku Doge]] spawns after 56.67 seconds<sup>1,700f</sup>.
*1 [[Aku Doge]] spawns after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Relic Bun-Bun]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Relic Doge]]s spawn, delay 50~60 seconds<sup>1,500f~1,800f</sup>.
**15 [[Relic Doge]]s spawn, delay 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Aku Doge]]s spawn, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
**15 [[Aku Doge]]s spawn, delay 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The Aku Altar will put a severe handicap on your units' levels if you haven't cleared any stages in [[The Aku Realms]].

This level plays very similarly to [[An Ancient Curse]], just with some [[Aku Doge]]s mixed in. Bring some sort of a shield piercer if you are paranoid of them, but if your attackers are used well, they don't add much difficulty to the fight anyway. The main problem is the [[Aku Altar (Enemy Base)|Aku Altar]], forcing you to progress quite far in (if not completely clearing) [[The Aku Realms]] to increase the level cap. Fully completing it is easily the best option, as your units' + levels will also be freed.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Maize Cat]] - A spammable meatshield that resists both Aku and Relic enemies. When paired with Research Combos, they make this level a joke.
*[[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]] - This duo goes just as hard here as they did in the original stage. They may not target Aku enemies, but they can still destroy hordes of Aku Doges, even without help from a Shield Piercer.
*[[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]] - His great DPS combined with his ability to slow both traits here with 100% uptime absolutely destroys this stage. He still works pre-[[True Form]], but he can't slow Aku, has less than half the effective health, and noticeably lower damage.
*[[Masked Yulala (Special Cat)|Spiritual Yulala]] - With his surprisingly-high health, somewhat-quick recharge time, and Massive damage towards Relics, he can serve as a replacement for Slapstick Cats in {{4c}}.

==Trivia==
*This is one of the only stages in the game that has a chance of rewarding a [[Battle Items#Treasure Radar|Treasure Radar]], the others being [[Villains Jungle]], [[Unkept Promises]], [[An Ancient Curse]], [[Reign of the Ape Lord]], [[Ape Lord's Revenge]] and [[Birth of True Man]].

